# Equinox counters a spell only if it would destroy a land you control (CR 608.2, 702.12b): Bot2's Cleansing Wildfire
# aimed at Bot1's Darksteel Citadel, which Equinox enchants, would not destroy it - it is indestructible - so it is not
# countered: it resolves, the Citadel stays, Bot1 declines the search and Bot2 draws its card.

[Bot1 Deck]
Darksteel Citadel
Mox Pearl
Equinox
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Cleansing Wildfire
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Darksteel Citadel.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Equinox.Cast(Darksteel Citadel)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Cleansing Wildfire.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Darksteel Citadel)
Bot1.Battlefield.Darksteel Citadel.Activate(Stack.Cleansing Wildfire; Ability: Counter)
Bot1.Decline

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Darksteel Citadel; Equinox; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Battlefield.Darksteel Citadel.Tapped = true
Bot2.Graveyard = Cleansing Wildfire; Black Lotus
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
